==English==

===Etymology===
{{OF.}} ''[[aquest]]'', French ''[[acquêt]]'', from Late Latin ''[[acquestum]]'', ''[[acquisītum]]'', for Latin ''[[acquisītum]]'', past participle (used substantively) of ''[[acquirere]]'' to acquire. See “[[acquire]]”

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{rare}} [[acquisition]]; the thing gained. [[w:Francis Bacon]].
# {{law}} property acquired by purchase, gift, or otherwise than by inheritance. - [[w:John Bouvier]].

====Usage notes===
Bouvier, 1856, [http://www.constitution.org/bouv/bouvier_a.htm] from which the Webster derives, uses the spelling "acquets".

